# Normalise every text file to LF, in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. The Content-Security-Policy pins the sha256 of the inline
# tag snippets in `client/index.html` (see server/_core/security-headers.ts),
# and the deployed document is built from the REPOSITORY bytes. Git's
# `core.autocrlf=true` - the default on Windows - rewrites LF to CRLF in the
# working tree, so a checkout on Windows computes a DIFFERENT hash for the very
# same snippet, the policy no longer matches what ships, and the test that
# guards the pair fails on one platform only. The same drift made two suites
# that read a source file as text (and search it for "\n") fail on Windows only.
#
# So the line endings are pinned here, for every platform, instead of being left
# to each developer's git configuration.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git detect binary files and leave them alone (the PNGs and
# the bundled `api/index.js` stay byte-for-byte identical); `eol=lf` makes the
# working tree match the repository everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf
